<block-guide name="core/table"><![CDATA[
CORE/TABLE
A static data table. Cells are read from the HTML; there are no inner blocks.

MARKUP (checked in the editor)
<!-- wp:table {"className":"is-style-stripes"} -->
<figure class="wp-block-table is-style-stripes"><table class="has-fixed-layout"><thead><tr><th scope="col">Plan</th><th class="has-text-align-right" data-align="right" scope="col">Price</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Basic</td><td class="has-text-align-right" data-align="right">$10</td></tr><tr><td>Pro</td><td class="has-text-align-right" data-align="right">$25</td></tr></tbody></table><figcaption class="wp-element-caption">Monthly prices</figcaption></figure>
<!-- /wp:table -->
Write the whole <figure> on one line, with no whitespace between tags.

STRUCTURE
<figure class="wp-block-table"> > <table> > <thead> / <tbody> / <tfoot> > <tr> > <th>|<td>.
Sections that have no rows are left out. Caption: <figcaption class="wp-element-caption">
after </table>, omitted when empty.

OPTIONS
hasFixedLayout defaults to TRUE: the <table> then MUST carry class="has-fixed-layout" (equal-width
columns). For auto-width columns set "hasFixedLayout":false and write <table> with no class.
Cell alignment: class="has-text-align-left|center|right" AND data-align="…" on that cell.
scope="col"/"row" is kept on <th> only. colspan / rowspan are plain cell attributes.
Stripes: className "is-style-stripes" in the comment and on the <figure>.
Colour and border settings are written on the <table>, not on the <figure>.

PITFALLS
A <table> without has-fixed-layout while hasFixedLayout is not false = invalid block.
Cells hold inline text (strong, em, a, br, code), never blocks.

CHECK
Reopen the editor: the table is editable cell by cell, no block-recovery warning.
]]></block-guide>
